  ('PF4','Sham contracting. Classification. Sham contracting occurs when an employer deliberately (or recklessly) misrepresents an employment relationship as an independent contracting arrangement, typically to avoid award/NES/super obligations. It is a distinct, separately penalised contravention from simple misclassification. Common questions: Could I get done for sham contracting even if I didn''t mean to? I genuinely thought he was a contractor — is that a defence? What''s the actual fine for getting this wrong? Are labour-hire and ''contractor'' the same risk?','[-0.027853,0.055133,0.004793,-0.059061,-0.045784,0.052487,0.011690,-0.072969,-0.023288,0.021538,-0.041936,0.049222,0.003064,0.046029,-0.032144,0.015901,0.030476,0.043337,-0.029354,0.023587,0.030089,-0.042644,-0.030326,0.020520,0.049736,-0.045017,0.057665,0.061206,-0.035256,0.015951,-0.099897,0.055931,-0.091188,-0.030405,-0.023056,-0.004775,-0.054926,-0.034785,0.009553,-0.067480,0.031524,-0.064239,0.002615,0.025874,-0.035100,0.054550,0.028712,-0.041774,-0.038315,-0.104073,0.054132,-0.028187,0.050486,0.077323,-0.041629,0.014481,-0.024380,-0.029426,-0.036408,0.089910,-0.012780,0.039524,0.017931,-0.028340,0.022267,0.014126,-0.051781,-0.014470,-0.010251,0.040884,0.029939,-0.107772,0.084822,0.003789,0.043823,-0.039320,0.032094,0.034842,0.065220,-0.164579,-0.018518,0.064845,-0.042709,-0.001921,0.000403,-0.113567,0.043465,0.064603,0.060815,0.011610,-0.013064,-0.072832,0.039072,-0.034000,0.056808,0.010099,-0.038763,0.143434,-0.071178,0.026726,-0.065922,-0.033344,-0.084653,-0.005731,0.046871,-0.004999,-0.023382,-0.012114,-0.005242,0.061192,-0.020192,0.025324,-0.033135,-0.033902,-0.043597,0.042258,-0.054176,0.056732,-0.107728,-0.008437,-0.001763,0.095395,-0.018465,0.072037,-0.040112,-0.127217,-0.082817,-0.000000,0.134910,0.031414,0.004801,0.019510,0.030581,0.032664,-0.015179,0.044034,0.068716,0.185590,0.005712,-0.022916,0.040139,0.029838,-0.051739,0.079856,0.051680,0.071828,-0.034534,-0.011053,-0.025288,0.017626,-