  ('PF5','Contractor high-income threshold & opt-out notice. Classification. A contractor earning above the "contractor high income threshold" ($190,100 for the year starting 1 July 2026) can give a written opt-out notice electing not to be assessed under the new whole-of-relationship test, preserving contractor status even if the relationship otherwise looks employee-like. The notice can be revoked once. Common questions: He earns good money, does that mean he''s automatically a contractor? What''s this opt-out notice thing my contractor mentioned? Can a contractor change their mind after opting out? Does the threshold change every year?','[-0.006624,0.094118,0.020453,0.031917,-0.038657,0.001435,0.008873,-0.019899,-0.016521,-0.001651,0.057620,0.006732,-0.021399,0.033127,-0.029699,0.010774,0.030811,-0.038528,0.016511,-0.059636,0.025228,0.007632,-0.070733,-0.002647,0.041794,-0.072177,0.059793,0.033348,0.001641,0.103057,-0.000374,0.104070,0.013987,-0.036825,0.054597,0.030035,0.022108,-0.015380,0.001655,-0.021004,-0.002899,-0.057391,0.022983,-0.006911,0.008906,0.001115,0.039135,-0.073764,-0.125794,0.023511,-0.000349,0.018109,0.003659,-0.026538,0.016277,0.012498,0.037827,-0.007776,-0.030266,0.070036,-0.068221,0.029465,0.006404,-0.028575,-0.032440,0.018849,0.012644,-0.081960,-0.020093,0.100634,-0.021637,-0.029437,-0.003839,-0.056404,0.130544,-0.008606,-0.014613,0.063987,0.065931,-0.107450,-0.049243,0.091045,-0.044680,-0.013869,-0.065307,-0.033676,0.039041,0.005631,0.064403,-0.014047,0.055127,-0.057986,0.026915,-0.004952,-0.038983,-0.011274,-0.017705,-0.056617,-0.086910,0.013095,-0.024683,-0.030920,-0.078021,-0.013729,0.014077,-0.012727,0.075988,0.052781,0.026723,-0.016463,-0.010544,0.001495,0.047390,-0.103145,-0.048099,0.074357,-0.022430,0.099976,-0.003902,0.034821,-0.013551,-0.019904,-0.050161,-0.036283,0.065674,-0.037286,0.017575,0.000000,0.160977,0.011157,0.003553,-0.020442,0.037703,0.011707,0.089118,0.024905,-0.017180,0.069128,0.061816,-0.001786,-0.018668,0.100477,-0