  ('PF14','Annual leave - accrual, excess, cashing out. NES/leave. Full-time employees accrue 4 weeks'' paid annual leave per year (5 for some shiftworkers), accruing progressively and carrying over indefinitely if unused. Awards may permit "excess leave" direction (requiring an employee to take leave when their balance grows too large) and cashing out of a portion of accrued leave under strict conditions. Common questions: He''s sitting on 8 weeks of annual leave — can I make him take some? Can I just pay out unused leave instead of her taking it? How much leave does a part-timer accrue? Does annual leave expire if it''s not used?','[0.037156,0.076251,0.055681,-0.021523,0.016531,0.049202,0.030385,-0.021193,-0.104953,0.006513,-0.008821,-0.036339,-0.070566,0.035446,0.011529,0.032592,0.021131,0.017269,0.012831,-0.052826,0.042481,-0.107150,-0.056769,0.026394,0.058262,-0.010762,0.027440,0.004338,0.035632,0.009638,-0.018847,0.045898,0.022319,-0.052313,-0.042577,0.027219,-0.013768,0.017091,-0.016225,0.023333,-0.053597,0.016313,0.059607,0.025334,-0.066741,-0.001516,-0.002344,-0.051762,-0.021145,0.085639,0.039887,0.001448,-0.013104,0.123590,-0.011629,-0.064041,0.084043,-0.084137,-0.045371,0.001877,-0.052648,0.026382,0.020843,-0.027301,-0.080723,-0.027527,-0.019291,-0.024540,-0.019443,0.072973,-0.051544,0.041580,-0.076901,-0.037562,0.047080,0.070562,0.034004,0.033281,0.033776,-0.024976,-0.031699,0.070067,0.068958,-0.039055,-0.003247,-0.015423,-0.042400,-0.009459,0.087714,0.034806,0.030856,0.066106,0.065319,-0.128994,-0.053842,-0.056927,-0.057221,0.026520,-0.045241,0.014206,-0.005318,0.081289,-0.016115,-0.014349,0.068176,0.016204,0.091627,-0.040681,-0.042432,-0.067168,-0.013231,0.040656,0.003868,-0.030450,0.083645,0.105747,-0.046940,0.012448,-0.025409,0.019325,0.045088,0.067303,-0.069525,0.034115,-0.094906,-0.014395,0.023202,0.000000,0.041428,0.010447,-0.000997,0.035053,0.044766,-0.008675,0.054818,0.005514,0.078209,0.016003,0.004605,0.047555,0.029210,-0.031856,0.077951,-0.004