  ('PF25','Payday Super (biggest 2026 payroll change). Payroll/super. From 1 July 2026, employers must pay super at the same time as wages (within a short window of each payday) rather than quarterly, moving to "Qualifying Earnings" as the calculation base and an annual (rather than quarterly) maximum contribution base. Late/short payments will trigger a revised, more immediate SGC exposure. Common questions: Do I really have to pay super every single payday now? What''s ''Qualifying Earnings'' — is that different to what I calculate now? How much time do I actually have after payday to get the super in? What happens if I''m late under the new system — is it worse than before?','[-0.088770,0.033773,0.022443,-0.015752,0.000632,0.016867,-0.043317,-0.013739,-0.093459,0.026300,0.002047,0.026724,-0.031078,-0.005148,-0.031695,-0.085448,0.028102,-0.050925,0.005307,-0.051068,0.027823,-0.097743,-0.037081,-0.051238,0.059872,-0.006871,0.010506,0.037433,0.075137,-0.000621,-0.054019,0.050081,0.005117,0.021450,-0.059793,-0.063798,0.018574,0.013372,-0.004485,-0.066676,-0.019282,-0.073394,-0.028947,-0.050213,-0.008035,-0.011724,0.039310,0.060693,-0.061765,0.076474,0.033349,-0.081876,0.008195,0.085318,-0.010746,0.076895,0.008188,-0.098333,0.057331,0.007250,-0.080377,-0.036492,-0.009667,-0.006763,0.059872,0.005137,0.000638,0.039900,-0.013823,0.112316,-0.042200,0.013059,0.041037,0.024772,0.081714,0.014241,-0.030998,-0.011233,0.055012,-0.040556,0.038664,0.021609,0.012157,-0.031802,0.023913,-0.049770,0.050512,0.093001,0.051211,-0.019523,0.068949,-0.044605,0.012584,-0.087509,-0.074881,-0.018178,-0.068595,0.008985,0.087941,-0.044920,0.042008,-0.055725,0.007460,-0.041151,0.044342,-0.011360,-0.052685,0.085070,-0.001597,-0.060739,0.018810,0.010019,0.107037,-0.062449,-0.045072,0.081533,0.005145,0.055864,0.009162,0.010956,0.063416,0.157258,-0.008510,-0.009178,-0.027851,0.079381,-0.036470,0.000000,0.059170,0.024334,0.039878,-0.096479,-0.008486,-0.043039,0.054939,0.028297,0.086559,0.012063,0.015