  ('PF26','Underpayment / wage-theft criminal offence + voluntary Code. Payroll/compliance. From 1 January 2025, intentional underpayment of wages/entitlements is a criminal offence (not honest mistakes), carrying penalties up to $7.825 million for companies and up to 10 years'' imprisonment for individuals. The Voluntary Small Business Wage Compliance Code (also from 1 January 2025) gives businesses with fewer than 15 employees a framework that, if followed, means the FWO cannot refer them for criminal prosecution — civil remedies may still apply, since strict liability continues to govern correct payment of award/NES/agreement entitlements regardless of intent. Common questions: Could I go to jail for a payroll mistake? What''s this Wage Compliance Code everyone''s talking about — do I need to sign up to something? Is an honest mistake treated the same as deliberate underpayment now? If I find I''ve underpaid someone, what should I do first?','[-0.084582,0.066136,-0.012975,-0.002900,0.025278,0.027044,0.010291,-0.034861,-0.040890,-0.022313,0.127895,0.006502,0.017544,-0.034287,-0.001924,-0.051235,0.048884,0.024640,0.021416,-0.038464,0.030605,-0.050373,-0.083460,-0.020114,0.088462,-0.061791,0.035980,0.022304,-0.024226,-0.036130,-0.022429,0.058250,0.069602,0.044863,0.030835,-0.020529,0.022617,-0.042007,-0.064705,0.012736,0.038359,-0.009957,-0.029313,-0.007390,-0.022449,-0.053779,0.014636,0.004345,-0.090768,-0.005125,0.038560,0.050408,0.032543,0.109925,-0.072653,-0.149580,0.017859,0.022064,-0.037451,0.000892,0.072589,-0.032149,-0.009299,-0.026581,-0.005060,0.007131,-0.042443,-0.057674,-0.063869,0.083032,0.011101,-0.098598,-0.035669,0.003183,0.046906,-0.014654,-0.052748,0.070783,0.035875,-0.077229,0.001952,0.013206,0.005735,0.032537,0.001815,-0.089075,0.008663,0.080387,0.121306,-0.010541,-0.008565,-0.031271,0.083076,-0.097772,-0.003241,-0.084822,0.019487,0.012185,-0.042603,0.007923,-0.029665,0.082586,-0.047211,0.003223,0.051776,0.047563,0.046789,-0.037788,0.001332,-0.03