  ('PF27','Self-correcting a discovered underpayment. Payroll/compliance. Where an SME discovers it has underpaid staff (commonly through an award/classification review, a payroll system change, or an external audit), there is an expected process: calculate the full extent using correct historical rates and hours, back-pay promptly, and — depending on scale — consider self-reporting to the FWO, which can lead to a cooperation agreement taking criminal referral off the table. Common questions: I think I''ve been underpaying someone — what do I do now? How far back do I have to go to fix this? Should I tell Fair Work myself or just quietly fix it? How do I even calculate what I owe going back years?','[-0.102148,0.062975,-0.025988,0.024198,-0.024096,0.035259,-0.024161,-0.005859,-0.042328,-0.030356,0.023516,-0.003171,0.008944,-0.051123,-0.070949,-0.024712,0.080844,0.040407,0.028862,-0.079695,0.010615,-0.034951,-0.067992,-0.044686,0.076568,-0.045061,-0.003979,0.021284,-0.066053,-0.072863,-0.013176,0.038924,0.063945,0.008663,0.006731,-0.041203,0.029556,-0.027600,-0.014642,-0.011678,0.014158,-0.037430,-0.018827,0.020893,-0.032427,-0.007213,0.041999,0.068046,-0.080408,0.065775,0.035950,0.024105,-0.002489,0.111367,-0.050369,-0.002232,0.070928,0.017161,-0.065204,-0.034160,0.043126,-0.011859,-0.063993,0.010876,-0.057774,0.055722,-0.037731,-0.056810,-0.077189,0.069965,0.015173,-0.070984,-0.027954,-0.011769,0.100734,-0.019233,0.005247,0.078583,0.070048,-0.087094,0.063042,0.088166,0.038133,0.032054,0.071801,-0.065773,0.002493,0.075179,0.089642,-0.019041,0.028987,-0.055260,-0.024632,-0.116375,0.053744,-0.053506,0.020761,0.061626,0.042404,0.030312,-0.029486,0.023634,-0.070745,-0.037936,0.009135,0.052759,0.020826,0.068081,0.050552,-0.016616,0.030801,-0.035286,0.003530,0.008790,0.039804,0.075349,-0.042112,0.074235,-0.060165,-0.050823,0.007281,0.122732,-0.018794,-0.005418,-0.091053,0.035743,-0.035293,-0.000000,0.015198,0.110202,0.011973,-0.064870,0.010367,-0.005163,0.048244,0.051351,