  ('PM1','Probation / minimum-employment-period confusion. Onboarding/probation. Owners routinely believe "probation" is a legal status that lets them dismiss freely in the first 3–6 months. In reality, probation is a *contractual* concept with no standing in the Fair Work Act; the only statutory clock is the **minimum employment period (MEP)** — 6 months generally, or **12 months for small business employers (<15 staff)** — before unfair dismissal protections switch on. A new starter accrues full leave and other NES entitlements throughout probation regardless. Critically, general protections and discrimination claims have **no minimum employment period at all** — an employee can be dismissed on day one and still bring a claim. Common questions: They''re still on probation, I can just let them go, right? We haven''t hit six months yet so we''re covered Do I need a reason if they''re still in their trial period? Can I extend probation if I''m not sure yet? Is probation even a real thing here?','[-0.012434,-0.000995,0.029913,-0.022723,0.036797,0.108771,-0.010588,0.036958,0.011177,0.015909,0.031030,0.098914,-0.056028,0.037058,-0.009995,-0.003704,0.095482,-0.027618,0.062480,-0.041049,0.084217,-0.059017,-0.056487,-0.014452,-0.044144,0.057567,-0.011847,0.034768,0.073166,0.002164,-0.026855,0.030886,0.099097,0.037508,0.011039,-0.004649,0.061496,-0.062139,0.005609,-0.054198,0.037320,0.012970,-0.036403,0.054912,0.048292,-0.005272,0.025014,-0.054177,-0.078282,-0.034684,0.080011,0.002565,0.047546,0.114353,-0.001015,-0.043658,-0.068383,-0.018457,0.018427,0.067745,-0.044369,-0.070286,0.027197,0.004107,0.066803,-0.046999,-0.044526,-0.030286,0.003043,0.045756,-0.147793,-0.033726,-0.031952,0.069521,-0.044831,0.038492,0.024937,0.018456,0.078363,-0.110947,-0.041798,-0.001488,-0.060306,0.019773,-0.089083,-0.076771,0.016151,0.012166,0.042202,-0.014967,0.100252,0.052463,-0.001875,-0.051108,-0.090020,-0.059324,0.041229,0.017246,-0.017329,0.018039,0.045436,0.014335,0.030240,-0.008434,-0.0