  ('PM3','Which policies are mandatory vs advisable. Policies. No Australian law mandates an "employee handbook" as a document. But a cluster of *obligations* effectively force documentation: WHS laws require systems for hazard identification, consultation and incident response; the positive duty under the Sex Discrimination Act effectively requires an anti-harassment policy as evidence of "reasonable steps"; privacy law requires a privacy policy once staff/customer personal information is handled; awards and the NES require documented leave, rostering and pay processes. SMEs conflate "no law says I need a handbook" with "I don''t need any policies," which is the trap. Common questions: Do I actually need a full handbook or just a contract? We downloaded a template years ago, is it still legit? What''s the bare minimum I need to not get caught out? Our policy folder hasn''t been touched since we started Is a verbal ''we don''t tolerate that'' enough?','[0.002305,0.049055,-0.029623,-0.031316,0.051125,0.108060,-0.028050,-0.046760,-0.001351,0.074121,0.029103,0.040977,-0.042748,0.076943,0.102190,-0.030764,0.017266,-0.078457,-0.016949,0.005730,0.013141,0.047239,-0.013195,-0.028780,-0.116835,0.005083,0.019843,-0.040245,-0.056976,0.047950,-0.022798,-0.032053,0.080292,-0.036135,0.043959,-0.023370,0.076400,-0.079787,-0.053445,-0.023648,-0.023313,0.018961,-0.109585,0.083130,0.008668,-0.014775,0.051417,-0.050499,-0.147512,0.027952,-0.024487,0.008234,0.081469,0.054963,0.054170,-0.032819,-0.008776,-0.016153,-0.003746,-0.067305,-0.033396,-0.063517,-0.094477,-0.020716,0.039576,0.034345,-0.065432,0.007412,0.042919,0.053915,-0.176314,-0.031654,0.053655,-0.008344,0.016065,-0.055015,0.026904,0.042257,0.069780,-0.113633,-0.097028,-0.001899,0.074934,0.032921,-0.060926,-0.026526,-0.047433,0.004708,0.047813,0.030735,0.020884,-0.031910,0.039606,-0.038445,0.023577,-0.041349,-0.007362,-0.040048,-0.070434,-0.026224,-0.050865,-0.036653,0.038714,0.125864,-0.029169,-0.005984,-0.061266,-0.047068,