  ('PM5','Designing & running a defensible PIP. Performance. A Performance Improvement Plan is not itself a legal requirement, but where used it must be procedurally fair: specific deficiencies, clear and realistic standards, genuine support/resources, a reasonable timeframe, and a clear (and honestly communicated) consequence if targets aren''t met. A dismissal following a PIP that was set up to fail, was unrealistic, or offered no real support is a significant unfair dismissal risk in its own right — the Commission scrutinises the *process*, not just the outcome. Common questions: We put them on a PIP but I think we''ve already made up our mind How long do we legally have to give them? What happens if they say they were never really supported? Do we need a written warning before the PIP or does the PIP count as the warning? They passed the PIP on paper but we still don''t think they''re right for the role','[-0.001093,0.052486,0.018948,0.019183,-0.016193,-0.026001,-0.056789,0.064357,-0.059159,-0.051451,-0.047233,0.070830,-0.015563,0.012516,-0.006418,-0.068943,0.090507,0.013782,-0.024090,0.010285,-0.012667,0.013279,-0.045667,0.077763,-0.091216,-0.009300,-0.053326,0.006239,-0.004472,-0.063878,-0.014090,0.002698,-0.008135,-0.035670,0.078736,0.045608,0.070762,0.007357,0.008629,0.006403,0.053408,-0.050293,-0.085949,-0.024655,0.060040,-0.028205,0.032516,-0.042901,-0.127481,-0.006524,-0.093529,-0.002060,0.043753,-0.058816,-0.041827,-0.002898,0.032104,-0.033455,-0.018391,-0.068368,-0.068332,-0.044963,0.005102,0.043535,0.017715,0.003962,0.005876,-0.066967,0.080546,0.054940,-0.019458,-0.048691,-0.071871,0.015250,-0.007580,0.016513,-0.018676,0.000475,0.004839,-0.031462,-0.017189,-0.020032,0.010265,0.031331,-0.017288,-0.026694,0.014707,-0.082884,0.041283,-0.054657,0.080906,0.043198,0.046466,0.035666,0.040789,0.069890,0.005274,-0.078778,-0.012116,0.069014,0.014183,0.031204,-0.046849,-0.049146,0.020046,-0.015410,0.003389,0.012479,-0.046828,-0.077378,0.068940,-0.107631,0.032466,