  ('PM6','Progressive discipline & procedural fairness. Discipline. Standard Australian practice is a graduated response — verbal warning, written warning, final written warning, then termination — proportionate to the issue, with each step requiring the employee be told the specific allegation, given a real chance to respond (commonly 24–48 hours'' notice of any meeting), and allowed a support person. SMEs frequently short-circuit this either by escalating too fast for minor issues or by avoiding action altogether until it becomes serious misconduct. Common questions: Is a text message warning enough or does it need to be a letter? How many warnings do I actually need before I can let them go? Do I have to let them bring someone to the meeting? This is the third time, can I skip straight to a final warning? We''ve never had to do this before, where do I even start?','[0.088657,0.074654,-0.000372,0.065816,0.046773,0.093090,-0.029483,0.003764,-0.011230,0.026506,0.070812,0.003811,0.029223,0.041933,-0.023769,0.026548,-0.008090,-0.045345,-0.033309,0.003861,0.033598,0.087869,0.028168,0.051742,-0.074194,0.033164,-0.014166,-0.022540,0.014036,-0.004734,-0.036227,0.036417,0.077541,0.017614,-0.019727,0.016380,0.041166,0.019144,-0.015961,-0.072611,0.030119,-0.049783,0.011582,0.057203,0.000793,-0.075210,-0.000224,-0.032174,-0.092969,-0.076959,0.023577,-0.057349,0.063841,0.045093,0.016397,-0.039787,-0.012480,0.010944,-0.049761,0.001932,-0.039403,-0.054934,-0.079946,-0.015564,0.022627,0.042301,-0.111166,0.036002,0.014237,0.111740,-0.106403,-0.075686,0.005462,0.090662,0.020929,0.005272,0.003630,0.037695,0.066596,-0.050991,-0.062179,-0.046331,0.065686,-0.001513,0.049456,-0.041580,0.058561,0.053546,0.030363,0.020258,0.065013,-0.000671,0.031891,0.027626,-0.115148,-0.028627,-0.129715,-0.066642,-0.047906,0.023836,0.016817,0.013762,-0.036713,-0.033425,0.005679,-0.075058,-0.006604,-0.038856,-0.072665,-0.059425,-0.002487,0.006093,-0.019203,-0.059163,0.063426,0.051557,-0.035302,0.102741,0.