  ('PM7','Serious misconduct / summary dismissal miscalls. Discipline. Summary (instant, no-notice) dismissal is legally available only where conduct is genuinely serious — theft, fraud, violence, or serious safety breaches are the Small Business Fair Dismissal Code''s own examples — and even then the employer must have reasonable grounds, not just suspicion. SMEs frequently over-call "serious misconduct" for things that are really performance or minor conduct issues, skipping process entirely because they believe summary dismissal removes the need for warnings. Common questions: This is gross misconduct, I can sack them on the spot, right? Do I still need to pay them out if I fire them for this? I caught them doing X, can I march them out today? Is swearing at a customer enough to skip the warnings?','[0.014386,0.115079,0.065095,0.050925,0.122694,0.045204,0.012139,0.009283,0.061774,0.020836,0.083199,0.031990,-0.004540,0.015357,-0.025849,-0.104477,-0.005175,0.053660,0.029526,0.031408,0.020498,0.021386,-0.053589,0.046667,-0.007052,-0.049005,0.004865,0.029979,-0.049385,-0.062239,-0.003439,0.094081,0.066254,0.052467,-0.008708,-0.068652,0.044616,-0.013458,0.020486,-0.062697,0.090584,-0.020600,0.002698,0.021295,-0.043302,-0.013833,-0.011689,-0.050955,-0.066877,-0.012477,-0.045724,-0.040764,0.010402,0.133248,-0.030389,-0.043554,0.008296,-0.075006,0.010811,0.028753,-0.020765,-0.019068,-0.009255,-0.032302,0.047292,0.024980,0.003415,-0.011560,0.056322,0.114858,-0.028582,-0.103358,-0.014664,0.064825,-0.058809,0.074951,-0.045961,0.021492,-0.002701,-0.022070,-0.100034,-0.074310,-0.042166,0.011324,-0.085314,0.015020,0.032007,-0.028421,0.070041,-0.054937,0.044618,0.001903,0.037091,-0.065255,-0.013957,-0.058266,-0.025145,-0.027715,-0.004005,-0.016648,0.058861,0.019472,-0.071435,-0.111259,0.056446,-0.061931,0.032912,-0.005348,-0.071974,-0.059332,0.002163,0.049788,0.002576,-0.036300,0.121265,0.086586,0.041938,0.020178,0.000716,-0.056003,0.035918,0.086863,0.005657,0.024463,-0.073185,