  ('PM9','General protections / adverse action. Termination. General protections (adverse action) claims are structurally more dangerous than unfair dismissal for SMEs because there is **no minimum employment period, no small-business exemption, no compensation cap, and courts can add penalties on top of compensation**. Performance management itself is repeatedly flagged as a "flashpoint": if an employee has recently exercised a workplace right (raised a safety issue, requested leave, made a complaint) and is then warned, performance-managed, or dismissed, the *timing alone* can support a claim regardless of whether the underlying performance issue was genuine — the onus shifts to the employer to prove the workplace right was **not** a reason for the action. Common questions: They only complained after we started managing their performance How do we prove we weren''t punishing them for that? There''s no cap on what we could have to pay? This feels like it could snowball into something huge We didn''t even know raising it was a ''workplace right''','[-0.018245,0.078920,0.045915,0.036911,0.110797,0.107095,0.009510,0.009645,0.001269,0.019500,0.064022,0.078432,0.007673,0.028464,0.052675,-0.044512,0.077404,0.077787,-0.002093,0.004802,-0.004359,-0.039708,-0.127766,0.026515,-0.088433,-0.048340,-0.016762,0.039242,0.005390,-0.090707,-0.040693,-0.002356,0.043318,0.013798,-0.050547,-0.014138,-0.060480,-0.002461,-0.031871,-0.083754,0.065089,-0.040064,-0.011046,-0.022185,-0.013366,0.040389,0.089252,-0.072245,-0.158959,-0.023261,-0.030152,-0.037168,0.029755,0.040794,-0.034297,-0.078395,0.018263,-0.059646,-0.038605,0.016775,0.003485,-0.089676,-0.081245,0.002025,0.053072,0.002368,0.031412,-0.016642,-0.018264,0.115456,-0.009731,-0.110789,-0.068965,0.089144,0.030794,0.068381,-0.043717,0.008830,0.020368,-0.029107,0.029281,-0.035718,-0.025282,0.019782,0.009704,-0.029853,-0.004164,0.014097,0.087206,0.010206,0.050425,0.006915,0.091494,0.006411,0.011367,-0.097310,-0.026694,-0.010899,-0.03