  ('PM10','Redundancy - genuine test & small-business exemption. Termination. Small business employers (<15 employees) are **exempt from statutory redundancy pay** under the NES — but this exemption has real limits: it doesn''t override redundancy clauses in an applicable award, enterprise agreement, or the employment contract itself, and notice (or pay in lieu) is still owed regardless. Separately, to be a *genuine* redundancy at all (protecting against an unfair dismissal claim), the employer must show the role is genuinely no longer needed, consultation obligations (where an award/agreement applies) were met, and redeployment was considered. Common questions: We''re under 15 staff so we don''t have to pay redundancy, do we? Is ''restructuring'' enough of a reason on its own? Do I need to consult if it''s just one role going? Their contract mentions redundancy pay, does that override the exemption? Can I make the role redundant and then just hire someone else to do it?','[-0.047331,0.050701,0.014039,0.012650,-0.013321,0.085504,0.005378,0.014624,-0.008225,-0.075469,0.034324,0.009150,0.037077,0.025978,0.022077,-0.049554,-0.012939,0.114951,0.005002,-0.081907,-0.017293,-0.039129,-0.106290,0.022773,0.050947,-0.052232,-0.000109,0.016687,-0.025744,-0.060199,0.028369,-0.001274,-0.004288,-0.004874,0.081336,-0.022279,0.006154,-0.023187,-0.042201,-0.035254,0.009628,0.013794,-0.047442,-0.010867,-0.013283,0.015502,-0.037214,-0.036949,-0.071243,0.018857,0.089528,-0.041498,0.040493,0.123982,0.010054,-0.045534,-0.039884,-0.012314,-0.068308,0.065933,0.008933,-0.041621,-0.082961,0.039136,0.051944,0.040471,-0.013263,-0.117060,-0.077720,0.043206,-0.029619,-0.102233,-0.065067,0.077328,0.043544,0.029763,-0.005358,0.053068,-0.003180,0.030729,-0.076780,-0.004901,-0.030275,-0.017372,0.005613,-0.095061,0.023589,-0.066023,0.027070,0.008433,0.084705,0.003736,0.063531,-0.014250,0.001834,-0.053954,0.003721,-0.018433,-0.041334,-0.027135,-0.005440,-0.013569,0.050184,0.046106,-0.004199,-0.003231,