  ('PM12','Flexible working arrangement requests. Flexible work. Eligible employees (e.g. parents, carers, over 55, experiencing family/domestic violence, or with a disability) have a statutory right under s.65 of the Fair Work Act to request flexible working arrangements, and employers must respond in writing within **21 days**, can only refuse on **genuine reasonable business grounds**, and — critically — must first **discuss the request and genuinely try to reach agreement** on alternatives before refusing. The Fair Work Commission now has expanded powers to arbitrate disputes about these refusals. Common questions: We''re too small to do a four-day week, surely that''s a valid reason Do I have to put the refusal in writing or can I just tell them? What counts as a ''genuine'' business ground? They want to work from home permanently, can I just say no? Now Fair Work can actually rule on this?','[-0.080246,0.050237,-0.009923,0.039885,-0.004513,0.055448,-0.033576,-0.029174,-0.058312,-0.026408,-0.001928,0.038404,-0.050224,0.064710,0.055415,0.009072,0.047096,-0.021946,-0.015054,0.050564,0.082934,-0.022654,-0.054029,-0.025053,0.003610,-0.032195,-0.038246,0.021078,0.049146,-0.047275,0.023657,0.065064,-0.011801,0.005602,0.086319,-0.019272,0.019961,-0.001046,-0.025949,-0.067919,-0.042243,-0.010525,0.003119,-0.051937,-0.033046,-0.016011,0.034365,-0.035526,-0.055068,0.029359,0.029741,-0.018037,0.014135,0.045751,-0.024600,-0.029450,-0.024013,-0.016785,0.019098,0.008237,0.018708,-0.096330,0.012374,-0.010020,0.000037,0.029191,-0.048869,-0.057929,-0.074663,0.003160,-0.039004,-0.022567,-0.076660,0.046448,0.105244,-0.041149,-0.019917,-0.031575,0.105553,-0.083805,-0.075225,-0.007764,-0.056305,0.084215,-0.002123,-0.106419,-0.003789,0.083417,0.152361,-0.009240,0.069542,-0.033818,0.002068,-0.053519,-0.014744,-0.077672,0.067357,-0.005722,-0.034282,0.011093,0.024838,0.016493,0.040193,-0.021773,0.015764,-0.065638,0.003447,-0.028023,-0.048026,0.015312,-0.031705,0.027010,0.043179,-0.0278