  ('PM13','Right to Disconnect in daily practice. Flexible work. The right to disconnect gives employees the right to refuse to monitor, read or respond to work contact outside working hours **unless that refusal is unreasonable**, weighed against factors like the reason for contact, how it''s made, and the employee''s role/circumstances. It commenced for large employers in **August 2024** and for **small business employers (<15 employees) on 26 August 2025** — meaning as at August 2026 it has been live for small business for exactly one year and is now a live, current obligation, not a future one. Common questions: Can I even text them about tomorrow''s shift after hours? Does this apply to us now, we''re small? What counts as ''unreasonable'' to expect a reply? We''ve always just called if something came up, are we breaking the law now? Do we need a written policy on this or just a chat?','[-0.014166,0.072325,0.013094,0.038371,0.031714,0.067403,0.022600,-0.072559,-0.032096,-0.054801,0.046999,0.124551,-0.057457,0.004677,-0.024611,0.023734,0.031389,-0.038944,-0.045451,-0.013259,0.017937,-0.020970,-0.097817,0.053476,0.023246,0.004130,0.072277,-0.029836,-0.005853,0.024221,-0.035121,-0.004082,-0.091427,-0.044264,0.002580,-0.026482,0.035332,0.025456,0.017036,-0.024699,-0.011370,-0.105615,-0.048586,-0.060756,-0.053373,0.072017,-0.039221,-0.018954,-0.021056,0.029268,0.014009,0.007132,0.012415,0.096859,-0.014493,-0.023888,0.021542,-0.036733,-0.000829,0.061610,0.047081,-0.037457,-0.040685,-0.006159,-0.022428,0.054622,0.016628,-0.025257,0.056125,0.013387,-0.094846,-0.036561,-0.024953,-0.018599,0.043928,-0.022614,0.038916,-0.033926,0.084807,-0.066192,0.003316,0.044129,-0.037256,0.025780,-0.077181,-0.003925,0.024810,0.029151,0.104658,-0.021248,0.032536,0.104105,0.051238,-0.014431,-0.041845,-0.115772,0.006991,0.053590,-0.038491,0.014726,0.065429,0.012833,-0.019781,-0.018859,0.010821,-0.048516,-0.013207,-0.064800,-0.019566,0.038043,-0.021289,0.027169,-0.083508,-0.034958,-0.00273