  ('PM14','Managing psychosocial hazards (new Code). WHS. Since 2022–2024 (varying by state, with the model Code finalised and Commonwealth version registered as a legislative instrument), WHS duty-holders must manage **psychosocial hazards** — poor workplace relationships/behaviours, high job demands, low job control, poor support, role ambiguity, remote/isolated work, violence and bullying — with the **same rigour as physical hazards**: identify, assess, control, and review, so far as reasonably practicable. This is now a mainstream compliance obligation, not a "nice to have" wellbeing initiative. Common questions: We don''t really have a WHS system, we''re only five people Is stress actually something we''re legally meant to manage now? What does a ''psychosocial risk assessment'' even look like for us? We just deal with bullying complaints as they come up Do we need external help for this or can we DIY it?','[0.013175,0.003032,-0.058146,0.028825,0.010577,0.044065,-0.009574,-0.008492,-0.080739,0.039333,0.074781,-0.010420,0.013393,0.063323,0.038774,-0.015792,0.007231,-0.081678,-0.033213,0.070031,0.061788,0.036369,-0.055402,0.059986,-0.123495,0.037530,-0.012121,0.015937,0.046735,0.022625,0.036948,-0.047322,0.012845,0.029493,0.015880,0.039676,0.021347,0.000357,-0.047301,0.006890,-0.026655,-0.025845,0.017585,0.018095,-0.007618,-0.040812,-0.008082,-0.081865,-0.107254,-0.043095,-0.015611,-0.007909,0.077070,0.046682,0.021902,-0.098024,0.078901,-0.050906,-0.080842,-0.023970,0.015541,0.001246,-0.010896,-0.001876,-0.015036,0.009101,-0.059029,-0.026069,0.034716,-0.011738,-0.092980,-0.118047,0.036101,-0.008484,0.016391,0.011845,0.005325,0.003230,0.120488,-0.060027,0.026800,0.007480,0.083650,0.062784,-0.026171,0.008718,-0.079136,-0.005632,0.075080,0.059372,0.020811,-0.060647,0.092135,0.037453,-0.026208,-0.036831,-0.004393,0.074877,-0.033881,-0.004725,-0.043344,-0.022995,-0.073353,0.081384,-0.021869,-0.054826,-0.015239,0.004041,-0.046824,-0.003370,-0.003913,0.087676,-0.008393,