  ('PM15','Officer due diligence & right-sized WHS. WHS. Directors/owners who meet the "officer" definition have a **personal due diligence duty** — active verification that the business has and uses appropriate WHS processes, not passive trust that "someone''s got it covered." For an SME this doesn''t require a heavy compliance bureaucracy but does require documented basics: a simple safety policy, hazard/incident reporting process, emergency procedures, risk assessments for higher-risk tasks, and genuine (even informal) worker consultation. Common questions: I didn''t realise that was on me personally, not just the business We don''t have a full WHS system, is that going to be a problem? What''s actually the bare minimum we need documented? Do I need to formally ''consult'' or is chatting at smoko enough? Who''s even responsible for this in a five-person company?','[-0.026740,-0.019595,0.029029,0.015552,0.067789,-0.040401,0.030259,-0.023743,-0.059120,0.075140,0.056160,-0.093929,-0.056367,0.005288,-0.020679,-0.013385,0.055524,-0.051163,-0.083254,-0.039723,-0.046510,-0.004084,-0.023881,0.072498,-0.127005,-0.035913,0.000904,0.009033,0.037621,0.008308,0.008844,-0.018642,0.085352,-0.054879,-0.022724,0.047322,0.077772,-0.018961,-0.015769,-0.022060,0.045403,-0.060060,0.016476,0.076671,-0.035547,-0.032199,0.049091,-0.054879,-0.090099,-0.024867,-0.071687,-0.065060,0.041749,0.020135,-0.052485,-0.042905,0.046782,-0.024193,-0.045553,-0.010273,-0.073941,-0.038031,-0.016740,0.028130,0.070480,0.020482,-0.051275,-0.055487,0.032376,-0.031819,-0.001230,-0.102324,-0.030401,0.040229,-0.024403,-0.029990,0.025911,0.019883,0.062566,-0.076595,-0.018073,0.055693,-0.002419,0.053573,-0.026200,-0.025458,-0.047175,-0.011405,0.032571,0.004702,0.114514,-0.084307,0.019140,-0.030280,0.042450,0.024892,0.000532,0.008678,-0.062045,-0.033607,-0.014315,0.014940,-0.090483,-0.002417,-0.019930,0.019166,0.000671,-0.017021,-0.029831,-0.009321,0.047016,0.030379,-0.019983,-0.021605,0.084294,-0.032144,-0.0398