  ('PM17','Retention & turnover. Culture. National turnover has actually fallen to a three-year low of **13.5% (June quarter 2026), down from 15.2% in December 2025** — an over-11% decline in six months — per AHRI''s Quarterly Australian Work Outlook. Despite this, engagement is weak: Gallup''s 2026 State of the Global Workplace put engagement at just **20%**, the lowest since 2020, with **managers identified as a major contributing factor**. The most cited reason employees leave is **excessive workload (26% of employers)**; the most-used retention levers are learning & development, flexible work, and wellbeing support (each cited by 36% of employers). Common questions: We just can''t compete with the bigger players on pay Everyone''s stretched too thin, that''s why people leave We don''t really do surveys, we just chat Losing one person here is like losing ten in a big company I don''t know why they left, they just said ''it''s not working out''','[0.069439,-0.061524,0.008174,0.085419,0.052610,0.063320,-0.015103,-0.049828,0.000224,0.006433,0.017106,0.035152,-0.039064,0.026037,0.015654,0.038996,-0.064635,-0.090994,-0.022620,-0.025566,-0.073374,0.001817,-0.028393,0.041090,0.059754,-0.015358,0.047245,-0.006698,-0.039163,0.021846,0.000339,0.079261,-0.005537,-0.056492,0.004645,0.016119,-0.026753,0.022790,-0.007570,-0.039530,0.048262,-0.027380,0.031900,-0.050849,0.012764,0.013762,0.012056,-0.027543,-0.063759,0.076646,-0.008823,0.000136,0.049444,0.026349,0.042758,-0.047780,0.028708,-0.079592,-0.023389,0.003007,-0.008762,-0.026464,0.025627,-0.023856,0.041645,-0.035296,0.001229,-0.048946,-0.094172,0.039563,-0.091298,-0.123042,0.008238,-0.052376,0.008462,-0.018967,0.073967,0.029698,0.149496,-0.040823,0.134270,-0.014171,-0.019641,0.068989,-0.091798,-0.098602,0.067188,-0.051428,-0.018155,0.020087,0.010718,0.060714,0.069108,-0.042829,-0.019915,-0.047624,-0.034305,0.039148,-0.096040,0.003930,-0.014671,0.097397,-0.014592,-0.039128,-0.093970,0.012115,-0.007983,0.003163,-0.024097,0