  ('PM18','Managing absenteeism without a system. Culture. Absenteeism costs Australian employers an estimated **$33 billion a year** (presenteeism a further ~$35 billion), representing roughly **7–8% of total payroll** for most businesses, or **$4,000+ per employee per year**. Workers take **9–14 days of unplanned absence annually** depending on industry (hospitality highest at ~11.9 days), and a striking **52% of Australian workers admit to taking at least one "not really sick" sick day** (ELMO Q3 2025 sentiment survey). Mental health is an increasingly cited driver: more than half of employers reported increased mental-health-related absence in 2025. Common questions: They always seem to be sick on a Monday I don''t want to be the bad guy but this keeps happening Is this actually a performance issue or a wellbeing issue? We can''t just roster around someone who''s out all the time Do I even have the right to ask why they''re off?','[0.076591,0.028343,0.002725,0.093037,0.053235,0.075151,0.047490,-0.080826,-0.023343,0.017064,0.038183,-0.055337,-0.009929,-0.020500,0.055790,-0.048729,0.022676,-0.092331,-0.020137,-0.003214,-0.064637,0.015570,-0.080167,-0.001267,0.058176,0.007038,0.065293,-0.003831,0.008398,0.026468,-0.020615,-0.011732,0.027886,-0.024249,0.096811,-0.028154,0.007291,-0.025619,-0.145016,0.011187,0.031055,0.085734,0.001686,-0.057865,-0.070440,-0.051529,-0.008146,0.059368,-0.005982,0.070182,0.036560,0.027452,0.072797,0.037116,-0.001873,-0.069418,0.054379,-0.110244,-0.108714,-0.021124,-0.037300,-0.025223,0.064293,-0.053945,0.033234,0.002211,-0.103306,-0.100239,0.001923,0.035074,-0.189737,-0.060006,-0.011956,0.019147,0.024255,0.010786,0.087874,0.034944,0.048341,0.012486,0.047122,-0.012524,0.017846,0.076574,0.036210,-0.063753,0.058615,0.065070,0.024195,-0.023346,-0.022663,-0.005841,0.044678,-0.053632,0.040918,-0.077959,0.004106,0.089533,-0.043057,0.002352,0.003369,0.054735,0.037997,0.065269,-0.024555,0.035252,-0.009730,-0.016628,0.016522,-0.031406,0.007158,0.