  ('PM19','Ad hoc training & key-person/succession risk. L&D. SMEs rarely have a training budget or framework; development happens informally ("learn on the job," occasional short course) and is the most-cited retention lever employers say they''re leaning on (36%, per AHRI data above) despite having no structured process to deliver it. Succession risk compounds this: specialised knowledge often sits with one or two people, and losing them has a proportionally larger impact than in a large organisation — yet formal succession planning is rare below a certain size. Common questions: We don''t really have a training budget, they just figure it out If Sarah left tomorrow we''d be in real trouble Succession planning feels like a big-company thing We can''t afford to send people on courses Everything''s in one person''s head','[0.020971,-0.030109,0.019804,0.035139,0.037181,0.031298,-0.080455,-0.020106,-0.005863,-0.013240,-0.006602,0.074700,0.042656,-0.016864,-0.036631,0.018012,-0.069094,-0.061771,0.014457,0.003144,-0.088043,-0.034717,-0.034204,-0.013975,0.046722,-0.083866,0.016492,-0.007602,0.011729,-0.042755,0.042148,-0.002016,0.044672,0.009996,-0.019541,0.062265,0.004292,0.025975,0.014548,-0.002201,0.064286,0.007649,-0.000891,-0.018731,-0.008642,-0.020478,-0.032157,-0.103453,-0.081527,0.006960,-0.051514,-0.108625,0.145820,0.051098,-0.088477,0.055150,0.014522,-0.048113,-0.066664,0.029910,-0.001261,-0.028683,-0.105636,-0.099622,0.013067,-0.051723,0.038925,0.046872,0.029114,0.038860,0.002813,-0.083766,-0.107115,0.089478,0.023338,0.085355,0.053529,0.019873,0.022803,-0.079264,0.009372,0.059789,0.015751,0.057247,-0.027391,0.000492,0.008620,-0.080078,0.003773,0.050873,0.003297,-0.013040,0.032457,0.021955,0.028178,0.104486,0.000333,0.017287,-0.041890,-0.005583,-0.041090,0.037586,0.005581,0.056888,-0.042946,-0.025649,-0.046035,-0.049993,0.083745,-0.010127,0.011831,0.043869,-0.015731,-0.003451,0.022952,0.078313,-0.126521,-0.030773,-0.042919,0.046410,-0.046520,0.012537,0.014473,-