  ('PM20','Positive duty (Sex Discrimination Act) at SME scale. DEI/harassment. Since the positive duty commenced, **all employers — with no small-business exemption of any kind** — must take "reasonable and proportionate" steps to eliminate, as far as possible, sex-based harassment, sexual harassment, sex discrimination and related victimisation. The AHRC now has active inquiry and enforcement powers, has flagged **retail trade and accommodation/food services as high-risk priority industries**, and continues to update small-business-specific educational tools. "Reasonable and proportionate" is scaled to the size and resources of the business — meaning the *standard* flexes for an SME, but the *duty itself* does not disappear. Common questions: Surely this doesn''t apply to a business our size What counts as ''reasonable steps'' for five staff? We''ve never had a complaint so we''re probably fine Do we need actual training or is a policy enough? Is this actually enforced against small businesses or just big ones?','[0.047461,0.098693,-0.029110,0.044989,0.023478,0.056353,-0.008845,-0.058581,-0.074115,0.039749,0.129916,0.008266,0.010443,0.060476,0.024982,-0.015705,0.107523,0.048488,-0.083012,0.025059,0.021131,0.017578,-0.015630,0.002879,-0.094538,-0.076356,-0.069834,-0.061836,0.001632,-0.097113,-0.024565,0.052476,0.155810,0.035431,-0.034988,0.041153,0.053760,-0.063238,-0.017808,0.003810,0.002943,-0.093587,-0.067486,-0.010619,-0.054822,-0.015136,0.077653,-0.050308,-0.051924,-0.063428,-0.000870,0.009203,-0.006275,0.031224,-0.046469,-0.048224,0.037336,-0.059170,0.025088,0.020658,-0.110592,-0.018813,-0.010996,0.006798,0.043339,-0.009771,-0.089515,-0.072697,-0.081473,0.060818,0.009998,-0.086001,-0.038438,0.085864,0.106595,0.023166,-0.047606,-0.008172,0.079760,-0.016822,-0.014748,0.020651,-0.030349,0.091400,0.011870,-0.063067,0.041536,-0.065255,0.102558,0.034440,-0.001376,-0.018388,0.034270,-0.013861,0.006169,-0.089786,-0.089618,0.008939,-0.057501,0.021311,-0.023303,0.07542