  ('PM21','Burnout & mental-health absence/presenteeism. Wellbeing. Around **half of Australian workers experienced burnout in the past year** (Beyond Blue, June 2025 national survey), and ELMO''s Q3 2025 index found **40% experiencing burnout right now** (~4.3 million workers nationally). Younger workers (18–29) report the highest rates, driven by workload, lack of management support, and inflexible conditions. Despite this, only **5% accessed an Employee Assistance Program** in the same period — a 35-percentage-point gap between prevalence and help-seeking. The Productivity Commission estimates a **$2.30 return for every $1 invested** in workplace mental health, and up to **$18 billion/year** in benefits from recommended reforms nationally. Common questions: Everyone''s just stretched thin, that''s normal for a small business though, right? We can''t afford an EAP I think they''re burnt out but I don''t know what to actually do about it Is this a performance issue or is something else going on? We don''t really have a wellbeing policy as such','[0.073260,0.031811,0.017412,0.118865,0.044978,0.130428,-0.044385,-0.030164,-0.049133,0.006039,-0.001669,0.042638,-0.019726,0.039036,0.043122,0.021509,-0.037391,-0.059249,-0.034413,-0.045999,0.007827,0.015506,-0.066100,0.056533,0.072397,0.026769,-0.035961,-0.018953,-0.026202,0.066476,0.005998,0.037797,-0.011775,0.004041,0.057079,0.002997,-0.015464,0.020464,-0.114325,0.034596,0.030244,0.001718,0.001484,-0.099234,-0.006741,-0.080166,-0.013501,-0.048691,-0.035951,0.067333,-0.032626,0.037021,0.114655,0.046652,0.068540,-0.044076,0.045619,-0.071468,-0.076895,0.020342,0.004724,0.010778,0.022700,-0.007700,-0.002468,0.010480,-0.082747,-0.053416,-0.049516,0.001974,-0.121112,-0.092858,0.025376,0.013019,0.043620,-0.024709,0.061373,0.006609,0.121690,-0.039269,0.073704,-0.024465,-0.022002,0.031270,-0.033561,-0.028945,0.102058,0.022450,0.014557,0.027842,-0.024947,0.032712,0.034687,0.001797,0.047160,-0.060019,0.010024,0.034172,-0.092878,-0.