  ('RA2','Choosing engagement type without misclassification risk. Workforce need. SMEs facing uncertain demand often default to "let''s just get a contractor" or "make them casual for now" to preserve flexibility. Australian law treats this as a substance-over-form question: if the working relationship looks like employment (set hours, supervision, sole client, tools provided), the law will treat it as employment regardless of the label or ABN. Common questions: Can I just get them on an ABN to keep it simple? I don''t want to commit to permanent yet, can we trial them as a contractor? What''s the difference between casual and part-time for me as the employer? If I get this wrong, what actually happens to me?','[-0.050011,0.009364,-0.048099,0.066878,-0.036240,0.111624,0.005562,-0.025319,0.011446,0.010678,-0.025151,0.010212,-0.027000,0.091622,0.116088,0.041773,-0.005230,-0.067139,0.024100,0.027291,-0.048196,0.031156,-0.068617,0.038960,0.017269,-0.069483,0.103912,0.043919,0.032666,-0.012996,0.034350,0.142741,0.010789,0.012503,0.061443,-0.049111,-0.039537,0.064552,-0.007956,-0.047396,0.007246,-0.030390,0.057058,-0.004427,-0.028914,-0.123684,0.085053,-0.028273,-0.089897,0.103210,0.031616,-0.044959,-0.035969,0.023098,-0.005742,-0.033157,-0.058479,-0.031149,-0.021317,0.022404,-0.031575,0.014401,-0.033655,0.002775,-0.008784,0.043594,-0.066183,-0.019272,-0.032703,0.006787,-0.022485,-0.151681,-0.043501,-0.072426,0.061300,-0.074216,0.032529,0.011318,0.038996,-0.073518,-0.004165,0.028361,-0.023005,0.007111,-0.031958,-0.058452,0.013794,0.040030,0.042961,-0.037281,-0.030431,0.009624,0.053738,-0.044400,-0.004577,-0.022934,0.004071,0.029087,-0.043003,0.055172,-0.074153,0.009540,-0.054137,0.044619,-0.078413,0.000721,-0.022011,-0.000193,0.110806,0.018799,-0.004537,0.031113,-0.015723,-0.057782,0.029502,-0.009914,-0.103470,0.040173,0.094238,0.008993,-0.042767,0.053041,-0.001799,-0.022596,-0.032808,0.029718,-0.001794,0.000000,0.005579,0.030647,-0.014520,0.066005,0.029041,-0.036319,0.0