  ('RA11','Setting a defensible pay band without enterprise data. Pay banding. SMEs need to decide what to pay for a role but typically lack subscription access to enterprise compensation data (Mercer, PayScale, etc.) and instead rely on a patchwork of the relevant Modern Award, competitor job ads, recruiter conversations, and gut feel. Common questions: What should I actually be paying for this role? Am I overpaying/underpaying compared to everyone else? The award says one thing but everyone in my industry pays more, what do I do? How do I know if $X is fair for a regional area vs the city?','[-0.022167,0.008232,-0.007410,-0.015101,-0.007822,0.065391,0.097206,-0.003742,-0.010105,0.015719,-0.055007,-0.050314,0.031249,-0.028569,-0.009155,-0.002369,0.089668,-0.021840,0.002286,-0.067238,-0.064012,-0.085997,-0.038855,-0.011028,0.110757,-0.073106,0.012117,0.019496,-0.046635,-0.066213,-0.014383,-0.004014,0.066005,-0.002679,-0.055567,-0.045295,0.011873,-0.058022,-0.149921,-0.017701,0.079743,-0.031374,-0.056510,-0.033697,-0.041905,-0.007724,0.118140,0.039820,-0.070557,0.080086,0.042940,-0.096540,0.046401,0.057218,-0.108787,-0.004766,0.048631,0.007802,-0.030353,-0.009453,-0.035557,-0.050041,-0.035608,0.058275,-0.036352,0.032962,0.012807,0.064569,-0.088337,-0.021900,-0.014877,-0.048196,0.020391,-0.034134,0.123334,0.056079,0.000040,-0.003924,0.060721,-0.021848,0.032324,0.009812,-0.046616,0.045958,-0.006618,-0.035157,0.039627,-0.012616,0.053408,0.006260,0.007767,0.070859,0.021880,-0.050409,0.030224,0.107266,-0.004528,0.001121,0.030511,-0.001123,-0.010428,-0.004101,0.026185,-0.006404,-0.030881,-0.068247,0.012593,0.034019,0.013947,0.003459,0.025418,-0.004411,0.038533,0.015084,0.038896,0.081045,-0.072366,0.072824,0.082305,-0.019026,-0.002375,0.074806,-0.049406,0.042115,-0.028616,0.045902,-0.061302,0.000000,0.008910,0.062028,0.068085,-0.084757,0.026552,-0.039047,0.026884,0.014681,-0.062258,0.054898,-0.033293,0.105198,0.045773,0.005496,0.008560,0.017928,-0.054707,0.078419,0.032420,0