  ('RA12','Whether/how to advertise salary (transparency). Pay banding. Whether to publish a salary range in the job ad, and if so, how (fixed figure vs range vs "circa"), is now a live decision for every SME ad, driven by candidate expectation shift and by SEEK''s own product-level nudges toward disclosure. Common questions: Do I really have to put the salary in the ad? If I put a number, will my current staff find out and want more? I don''t want people just applying for the money. Competitive salary" is easier to write than a number." [illustrative reasoning, not a literal quote]','[-0.044874,0.030052,-0.068071,0.017526,0.028753,0.035668,0.063574,0.007147,-0.000464,-0.045737,-0.046245,-0.057176,-0.020361,-0.048114,0.064458,-0.051175,0.055213,0.060629,0.040843,-0.028053,0.052201,-0.007263,-0.003542,-0.046448,0.080216,-0.147831,0.062168,0.023522,-0.026709,0.029111,0.000531,-0.008272,0.098481,-0.042929,0.030152,-0.088859,-0.042257,-0.002196,-0.049878,0.068473,0.033514,-0.079118,-0.056188,-0.063047,-0.064613,-0.025825,0.093376,0.108807,-0.082621,0.059482,-0.015527,-0.083630,-0.001156,0.010574,-0.109325,-0.067865,0.003043,-0.011533,-0.035010,0.044442,-0.045315,0.019332,-0.072623,0.048793,0.089131,-0.024236,-0.008755,-0.009891,-0.036740,-0.044514,0.019370,0.037109,-0.054663,-0.043680,-0.007287,0.027455,-0.001947,0.014414,0.026048,-0.034612,0.086139,-0.083045,-0.098477,0.042204,0.023073,-0.056150,0.090926,-0.000052,0.012691,0.001417,0.020255,0.085869,-0.047667,-0.008215,-0.015612,0.023088,-0.029632,0.045658,0.054119,-0.008760,-0.106149,-0.042789,0.077773,-0.050686,0.000125,-0.005088,0.024176,0.088417,0.045181,0.035547,0.006092,0.047303,0.003003,-0.007963,0.083817,-0.025434,-0.058775,0.013982,0.052197,-0.044668,0.054472,0.038019,-0.016652,-0.008307,-0.018620,0.016977,-0.009782,-0.000000,-0.001107,0.030052,0.044430,0.024939,0.018592,-0.011541,-0.032446,-0.027960,0.060503,0.045891,0.008134,0.028030,0.059598,0.066345,0.035474,0.046312,0.040911,0.028784,0.020129,0.066422,0.0