  ('RA14','Gender pay equity exposure below WGEA threshold. Pay banding. Formal WGEA gender-pay-gap public reporting only applies to employers with 100+ employees (covering roughly 5,000–8,500 employers nationally), meaning the overwhelming majority of Australian SMEs are not required to report. However, the underlying legal obligation — equal remuneration for work of equal or comparable value under the Fair Work Act — applies regardless of employer size, and reputational/candidate-facing pay-equity expectations increasingly flow down to SMEs regardless of the reporting threshold. Common questions: We''re way under 100 staff, so this doesn''t apply to us, right? I just pay people what I negotiated with them individually, is that a problem? Do I need to worry about pay equity if we''re small?','[0.052050,-0.018444,-0.073660,0.042725,-0.014432,0.044174,0.004686,-0.065197,-0.042242,0.065677,-0.003368,-0.044460,-0.038249,0.011658,0.069828,0.006794,0.027438,-0.010554,-0.028865,-0.056083,0.009786,-0.023197,-0.001195,-0.065864,-0.050220,-0.094665,-0.016337,0.036761,-0.005182,0.012447,-0.004535,0.050886,0.054054,0.006014,0.023346,-0.011331,0.017354,-0.061873,-0.002471,-0.019876,0.038147,-0.007551,-0.003104,-0.004870,-0.109639,0.046486,0.061638,0.050599,-0.118322,0.043163,0.040411,-0.060688,0.020449,0.115516,-0.076899,-0.126361,0.019885,-0.050109,-0.012327,-0.000168,-0.088550,-0.037874,0.006430,0.021310,0.079811,0.000127,-0.102133,-0.023276,-0.046621,0.012811,0.005028,-0.026361,-0.077316,0.025674,0.069599,0.056494,0.041545,0.043983,0.063495,-0.027028,-0.009794,-0.018142,-0.002584,0.035972,-0.012651,-0.102925,0.058255,0.013411,0.041762,0.037496,-0.050894,-0.004690,0.069749,0.043838,0.046412,-0.044899,-0.023592,0.012378,-0.064615,0.006011,-0.055954,-0.014889,0.093784,0.010458,-0.083717,-0.007437,0.077846,0.037669,-0.094655,-0.046937,0.034828,0.061999,0.044893,-0.024833,0.047751,-0.050630,0.048295,0.095796,0.047924,-0.086461,0.052279,0.035798,-0.051311,-0.054180,0.064545,0.0743