  ('RA16','Reading a bifurcated market. Sourcing. SMEs need to calibrate expectations to the specific occupation and region they''re hiring into, not the aggregate national narrative. Aggregate indicators (more applications per ad, longer hiring timelines, softer ad volumes) suggest an easing, employer-favourable shift, but this masks acute, persistent shortages in health, trades, and some professional/technical occupations. Common questions: Everyone says it''s easier to hire now, why am I still struggling to find a [tradesperson/nurse/technician]? I''m getting heaps of applications but none of them are qualified. Is now a good time to hire or should I wait? Why do I have to pay so much more than last year for the same role?','[0.022939,-0.099531,0.085927,0.088204,0.076879,0.054369,-0.050586,0.032880,0.009575,-0.052819,-0.127914,-0.068486,-0.040258,-0.007379,-0.031726,-0.010012,-0.030867,-0.013050,0.053035,-0.059631,-0.152036,-0.004062,-0.075360,-0.110692,0.033915,-0.021110,-0.029665,-0.030319,-0.006838,0.036883,-0.027522,0.133775,0.078820,0.032517,0.052279,-0.012996,-0.033888,0.052732,0.011216,-0.022446,0.083626,-0.060538,-0.005312,0.004983,-0.022131,-0.055809,0.102118,-0.009113,-0.030131,-0.019032,-0.032417,-0.011834,0.053971,0.043146,-0.035500,0.042640,-0.020779,-0.002209,-0.033874,0.027191,-0.044580,-0.031341,-0.019897,-0.006872,0.096884,-0.055444,-0.019737,0.055820,-0.080780,-0.005388,-0.043657,-0.039766,-0.113467,0.014483,0.088964,-0.048185,0.033844,-0.005133,0.088394,0.000456,0.001382,-0.049511,-0.080177,0.052706,-0.007697,0.008986,0.002060,-0.032419,-0.004040,0.017217,0.034818,-0.004388,-0.023630,0.013802,0.115266,0.030079,0.018594,0.124236,0.032442,0.049420,-0.000724,-0.022496,0.054217,0.019255,-0.100780,-0.045903,-0.023201,0.020899,-0.051792,0.016278,-0.000289,0.014796,-0.014379,-0.002318,-0.032469,0.019184,-0.020756,-0.043204,-0.031482,0.107001,-0.066626,0.044268,-0.073519,-0.032078,0.047624,0.107653,-0.009641,0.000000,0.043449,0.027023,0.001461,0.032419