  ('RS7','Unlawful / discriminatory interview questions. Interview design. Hiring managers without HR training routinely ask questions that are unlawful or high-risk under Australian anti-discrimination law — about age, marital/family status, pregnancy plans, health, religion, or country of origin — usually with no discriminatory intent, simply trying to "get to know" the candidate or assess availability/reliability. Common questions: just wanted to know if she''s planning a family," "asked if he could handle the physical side of the job," "wanted to make sure they could work weekends so asked about kids," "just making conversation," "didn''t think it was a big deal.','[-0.006901,0.110198,-0.069495,0.076988,0.046715,0.053055,0.036605,-0.095916,-0.053792,0.009098,0.009666,-0.052330,-0.030523,0.028179,0.042348,0.002415,0.063310,-0.074070,-0.012023,0.043395,-0.017914,0.019843,0.011870,-0.009365,-0.038011,-0.043624,0.088474,0.045967,0.035606,0.065474,0.008545,0.049878,0.054074,0.089502,0.077667,-0.037358,-0.018582,0.012399,-0.011551,-0.010938,0.010545,-0.068349,-0.027409,-0.022940,-0.065530,-0.066728,0.047495,-0.000807,-0.076752,-0.008807,-0.095421,-0.059351,0.058638,0.011332,-0.017970,-0.046642,-0.022818,0.025628,-0.083655,0.026632,-0.025826,-0.080298,-0.054433,0.054023,-0.067022,0.033326,-0.101221,0.044594,0.083792,-0.013823,-0.090218,-0.060574,-0.105432,0.071574,0.024435,-0.001075,0.054190,-0.045465,0.047258,-0.033838,-0.037023,-0.083621,-0.012369,0.038640,0.028043,0.008611,-0.009645,0.000396,0.023272,-0.023701,-0.051767,-0.022611,0.048664,-0.024391,0.107095,-0.015051,-0.031129,0.016238,-0.050381,0.022080,0.040527,0.003844,-0.057940,0.100063,-0.051550,-0.016210,-0.042313,-0.025162,0.000668,-0.005998,-0.022281,0.034553,0.031284,0.011580,-0.037362,0.015213,0.033507,0.083336,-0.081865,-0.008276,0.004173,0.003971,-0.024189,-0.019619,0.008375,-0.096665,-0.062814,0.000000,0.039395,0.029468,0.066308,-0.012000,0.012948,0.044589,0.006579,0.013699,0.147725,0.091076,0.048142,0.