  ('RS9','Interview scorecard design & panel calibration. Interview design. Where SMEs do use interview scorecards, they''re often poorly designed (too many vague criteria, no anchored rating scale) and, in panel interviews, scored via open group discussion rather than independent scoring followed by calibration — which allows the first or most senior voice to anchor everyone else''s assessment. Common questions: we all just talked it through," "the boss decides anyway," "we compare notes after," "everyone kind of agreed," "went with the room.','[-0.005903,0.048496,-0.047255,0.049809,0.093657,0.003416,0.035380,-0.008413,0.044784,-0.034382,-0.072513,-0.002175,-0.030289,-0.012092,-0.000608,-0.075870,0.003917,-0.054504,0.026418,-0.008016,-0.072351,0.014145,0.016849,-0.060895,-0.012188,-0.001191,-0.087129,0.020593,0.047965,-0.027468,0.009460,0.070324,0.179632,0.063326,-0.049986,-0.004325,0.003331,0.007791,-0.048861,-0.006868,0.012918,0.019512,0.049273,-0.001376,-0.028919,-0.108633,-0.067345,-0.040381,-0.101966,0.055120,-0.118110,-0.035914,0.006383,-0.036120,-0.004685,0.076617,-0.007830,-0.002665,0.000743,-0.018077,-0.064430,-0.066446,-0.038310,0.085226,0.114717,0.011432,0.011843,0.008199,-0.046787,-0.013080,-0.046545,0.000173,0.059658,0.032235,0.056609,0.053974,-0.067126,-0.058502,0.069109,0.028061,-0.076168,-0.071446,-0.030745,0.017955,0.080288,-0.010602,0.044460,-0.021514,0.034451,0.023652,-0.001608,0.015715,-0.063261,0.028192,0.056973,0.038788,-0.037238,0.027353,0.026401,-0.005743,0.025817,0.067071,-0.006456,-0.027807,-0.018766,-0.041775,0.016128,0.007240,-0.009981,-0.022241,-0.065214,-0.005972,0.088839,-0.036981,0.007518,-0.089060,-0.001145,0.022542,0.034091,0.023945,0.016945,0.006075,-0.040065,-0.066656,-0.031831,0.071839,-0.015474,0.000000,0.035564,0.009417,0.009570,0.039844,-0.007173,0.010984,-0.091084,0.082615,-0.000999,0.050150,0.049335,-0.004939,0.026316,0.101625,0.088352,0.083619,-0.089998,0.069761,-0.088637,0.024735,0.031855,-0.033775,0.052157,0.004707,0.099