  ('RS10','Disproportionate/irrelevant psychometric testing. Assessments. SMEs sometimes apply generic personality or cognitive tests to every role regardless of relevance, either because a recruitment platform bundles them in by default or because a manager believes more testing equals more rigour. Used disproportionately, this adds cost, slows time-to-hire, and can introduce discrimination risk if the test isn''t validated for the role or disadvantages particular groups. Common questions: we run everyone through a personality test," "it gives us a fit score," "makes the process feel more scientific," "not sure what the numbers actually mean, but it feels thorough," "the software recommended it.','[0.027248,0.050495,0.028963,0.079878,0.084024,-0.009291,0.051303,0.037220,-0.009991,-0.002730,0.014366,-0.042058,-0.022823,0.001759,0.021193,-0.034035,0.027673,0.029876,0.007527,0.036662,-0.074873,-0.071529,-0.045223,-0.059538,-0.038721,-0.061584,-0.058650,0.002029,-0.018524,-0.028786,0.069464,0.123757,0.016105,0.135804,-0.010647,-0.011228,-0.006890,0.067166,0.006581,-0.014689,0.039832,-0.029333,0.035832,-0.005755,-0.028759,-0.071389,-0.082905,0.012948,-0.130557,-0.065912,-0.127955,-0.069548,0.031685,0.039288,-0.038120,0.002265,0.043678,0.009283,-0.052736,0.014442,-0.064704,-0.051048,-0.047426,-0.005610,0.096014,0.055985,-0.013433,-0.068691,0.000543,-0.009965,-0.033448,-0.060357,-0.004901,0.059216,0.097435,0.044295,-0.037063,-0.044271,0.052513,0.050919,-0.045295,0.028328,-0.033708,-0.003014,0.067767,0.042237,0.017289,-0.083062,-0.003388,0.067449,-0.006666,-0.017259,-0.046052,-0.020305,0.009323,0.031152,-0.036356,0.048041,-0.016191,-0.006805,0.051243,0.028646,-0.026493,0.029883,-0.059455,-0.054557,0.064602,-0.081549,0.015104,-0.056871,-0.049550,0.023585,0.066975,-0.012373,0.002011,-0.036599,-0.038335,0.125531,0.002972,0.022250,0.036305,0.047561,0.041064,-0.005594,0.016855,0.101792,-0.052709,0.000000,0.002857,-0.034625,0.036734,0.057139,-0.065027,-0.011998,-0.050899,0.05987