  ('RS11','Reasonable adjustments in assessments (disability). Assessments. Where skills tests, timed assessments or interviews aren''t adapted for candidates with disability, SMEs risk both excluding capable candidates and breaching the Disability Discrimination Act 1992. Reasonable adjustment could mean extra time, an alternative format, or a different assessment method altogether that still measures the same job-relevant capability. Common questions: didn''t know we had to do that," "we just run the standard test for everyone," "didn''t want to single anyone out," "they didn''t mention anything so we assumed it was fine.','[-0.013362,0.036585,-0.015540,0.072127,0.107095,0.041641,-0.039310,0.034476,-0.073238,0.017392,0.051285,0.011684,-0.015957,-0.006573,-0.059235,-0.018634,0.006226,0.006895,-0.011429,0.087256,-0.046628,0.028993,-0.028691,-0.000475,0.005503,-0.042762,-0.062089,0.031062,-0.008768,-0.017672,-0.014985,0.022554,0.034494,0.025702,0.023607,0.015850,0.039269,0.028340,-0.000924,-0.053298,0.005119,-0.081733,-0.029240,-0.090263,-0.055393,-0.055481,0.026312,-0.087722,-0.137716,0.004099,-0.050694,-0.002307,0.018542,-0.038936,-0.077679,0.035430,-0.004356,0.016807,0.051099,-0.015324,-0.088992,-0.079396,0.021784,0.053452,0.084372,0.022236,-0.050733,-0.089851,-0.014990,-0.016011,-0.058067,-0.006183,-0.057996,0.057104,0.123621,-0.023163,-0.010811,0.018298,0.085144,0.014604,-0.043042,-0.007648,-0.035349,0.019333,0.074924,-0.013422,-0.033779,0.007079,0.023222,0.011172,0.064036,-0.070201,-0.057384,0.030059,0.069686,-0.071403,-0.004664,0.020877,-0.004998,0.002367,-0.000401,0.058228,-0.066256,-0.044863,-0.056226,-0.054984,0.070791,-0.081973,-0.056381,-0.050069,0.033439,-0.021228,0.011344,-0.027172,0.002401,-0.061909,-0.034706,0.020831,0.006310,-0.066610,0.000517,0.023609,0.002066,-0.058643,0.038358,0.047318,-0.011052,0.000000,0.055168,-0.004230,-0.012295,-0.075517,0.009278,-0.089831,-0.047670,0.012999,0.064088,0.015287,0.097876,0.104856,0.058566,-0.112016,0.029525,0.06