  ('RS17','Probation period misunderstanding. Offer. SME employers frequently conflate the contractual probation period with the statutory minimum employment period for unfair dismissal protection (six months generally, 12 months for a small business employer with fewer than 15 employees), and mistakenly believe that dismissing someone "during probation" automatically shields them from all legal risk. Probation is a contractual concept the Fair Work Act does not define or require; general protections (adverse action) apply from day one regardless of probation status. Common questions: they''re still on probation, so we can just let them go," "no risk while they''re on their trial period," "haven''t passed probation yet so it''s fine," "three-month trial.','[-0.031567,0.053732,0.052803,0.032291,0.039131,0.096433,0.033749,0.005675,0.021305,-0.013065,0.066351,0.121359,-0.034298,0.001455,0.020180,-0.003462,0.015662,0.008511,0.002465,-0.040415,0.040055,-0.027477,-0.086797,-0.019709,-0.066518,-0.013571,-0.037775,0.012904,0.017678,0.039771,-0.051686,0.029378,0.047491,0.039917,0.014426,-0.038395,-0.009741,-0.030340,0.002871,-0.118997,0.054378,0.019640,-0.011704,0.001332,-0.006474,-0.066927,0.017424,-0.108000,-0.066219,-0.015770,0.022442,-0.073525,0.043416,0.092787,-0.022672,-0.056577,-0.078027,-0.051801,0.018607,0.014828,-0.042834,-0.101370,-0.038675,0.019795,0.015666,-0.015275,-0.032894,-0.029142,0.015956,0.089064,-0.118549,-0.053470,-0.056311,0.106906,-0.033965,0.084402,-0.010145,-0.013274,0.067975,-0.079153,-0.030276,-0.005310,-0.046221,0.010536,-0.083400,-0.049428,0.014925,-0.014813,0.073604,-0.031137,0.084239,0.066414,0.012753,-0.047030,-0.050525,-0.104389,0.035749,0.018500,-0.024979,0.068265,0.060486,0.041918,-0.022672,-0.064147,-0.042068,-0.054386,0.016218,-0.032208,-0.081453,0.034408,-0.014037,0.032981,0.053986,-0.044056,0.010909,0.074936,-0.094599,0.060238,-0.013592,-0.038211,-0.033345,0.102513,0.000101,-0.011555,-0.048402,0.051117,-0.057854,0.000000,0.056765,-0.10