  ('RS18','Counter-offers & lost candidates at the eleventh hour. Offer. SMEs frequently lose a preferred candidate at final-offer stage when the candidate''s current employer counters to retain them — or the SME itself, needing to retain a departing staff member, makes an ultimately ineffective counter-offer. Evidence suggests counter-offers are a weak long-term retention fix in either direction. Common questions: they got counter-offered and pulled out," "lost them to their current employer at the last minute," "gutted, we thought it was locked in," "should have moved faster on the offer," "meeting salary expectations is our biggest headache.','[-0.113308,-0.040805,0.071260,0.067017,0.060171,0.100014,0.040019,0.014205,0.061994,-0.010584,-0.004134,0.058290,-0.041391,-0.051826,0.015290,-0.017329,-0.044706,-0.028551,0.025316,-0.010372,-0.118104,0.009197,-0.033349,-0.041563,0.064991,-0.086074,-0.010600,0.044040,0.003955,-0.006765,0.006615,0.044920,0.016808,0.060376,0.033371,-0.002366,-0.090503,-0.029538,-0.000712,-0.038714,-0.016510,-0.063857,-0.071691,-0.067986,-0.042603,0.023222,-0.037522,0.010532,-0.050799,0.046048,0.014668,-0.068548,-0.004535,0.062960,-0.001793,0.090818,-0.016253,-0.045236,-0.007585,0.077168,-0.001809,-0.112967,-0.116113,0.028296,0.033573,0.031595,-0.059732,-0.018336,0.004893,0.069744,0.021519,-0.033197,-0.075754,0.022662,0.010121,0.069125,0.014156,-0.055699,0.050055,0.006631,-0.055061,-0.063764,-0.090840,-0.049145,0.017091,-0.073079,0.024838,-0.015652,0.071128,0.004146,0.029398,0.016714,0.041145,-0.020921,0.006778,0.019537,0.007637,0.147942,-0.034370,0.014729,0.039088,0.081233,-0.063984,-0.022590,-0.050069,-0.087832,-0.006660,-0.029193,-0.014514,0.003586,-0.011377,0.018594,0.060734,0.024504,-0.039000,0.042375,-0.032314,0.057752,0.029543,-0.042140,-0.032903,0.038347,-0.017552,-0.084331,-0.066526,0.084088,-0.015292,0.000000,-0.056886,-0.054058,-0.053590,-0.029945,0.015144,-0.073063,-0.047132,0.055547,-0.057374,0.071259,-0.007846,0.069534,0.005571,0