  ('RS23','Privacy Act ADM transparency rule (from 10 Dec 2026). AI-in-hiring. Australia''s Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the Australian Privacy Principles (APPs) apply to any AI recruitment tool that processes personal information (names, contact details, resumes, interview recordings, assessment results). A significant new obligation — Automated Decision-Making (ADM) transparency under new APP 1.7-1.9 — commences 10 December 2026, requiring organisations to update their privacy policies to disclose the kinds of personal information used in ADM and the kinds of decisions involved. Regulatory commentary explicitly identifies "deciding whether to give an applicant an interview" as likely falling within scope. Common questions: didn''t know we needed a privacy policy update for that," "the software handles the data, not us, surely," "what does ''automated decision'' even mean here," "we just use whatever the platform gives us.','[-0.077648,-0.010267,-0.020314,0.004855,0.058475,0.031882,0.049878,-0.025805,-0.045450,0.053452,0.049690,-0.018008,-0.015550,-0.021395,0.072155,0.029057,-0.016039,-0.047966,-0.038071,-0.028778,0.034126,0.062347,-0.033518,-0.037922,-0.024535,-0.027316,0.067630,-0.051444,0.012039,0.018161,0.039279,0.010488,0.061629,0.050105,0.021097,-0.056373,-0.067859,-0.048557,-0.020498,-0.017769,0.025316,-0.101329,-0.043746,-0.025165,-0.003682,0.027794,0.060228,0.000936,-0.050935,0.040916,-0.080416,-0.016255,0.008912,-0.012183,-0.060312,-0.056094,0.003585,0.003940,-0.119739,0.001832,-0.013011,-0.074331,-0.045862,0.057825,0.011148,0.139195,-0.064712,-0.043100,0.039760,-0.030481,-0.050969,0.003368,-0.005437,0.032447,-0.011610,0.012383,-0.029787,0.058444,0.016306,-0.029451,0.001045,-0.098176,-0.004239,0.019514,-0.015909,-0.013552,-0.005651,-0.044609,0.044522,0.032820,0.043822,-0.091277,0.031273,0.050524,-0.018391,-0.098163,-0.018474,0.036651,-0.008968,-0.017622,-0.073699,0.056848,-0.068945,0.034507,-0.026063,0.050172,0.025165,-0.051024,0.049946,0.092453,0.008805,-0