  ('RS24','Employee-records exemption uncertainty ("tranche two"). AI-in-hiring. Currently, s.7B(3) of the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) exempts private-sector employers from most Privacy Act obligations for acts and practices directly related to an existing employee''s employment relationship — but this exemption does not cover job applicants/candidates, who are already fully protected. The exemption''s future is itself uncertain: "tranche two" of Privacy Act reform, expected later in 2026, is actively considering narrowing or removing the employee-records exemption, alongside possible removal of the small-business exemption. As at 2026-08-10 these changes are proposed/under consultation, not law. Common questions: thought employee data was exempt anyway," "wasn''t sure if that applied before they started," "heard the exemption might get scrapped," "waiting to see what happens with the reform before we build anything new.','[-0.095420,-0.011694,0.041954,-0.008092,0.031111,0.063654,0.044519,-0.049695,-0.074100,-0.021561,0.069783,0.046166,0.001495,-0.061179,0.047217,-0.005238,-0.031203,0.005839,-0.021503,-0.022893,0.050158,-0.047543,-0.121832,-0.006751,0.023659,-0.015012,0.021452,-0.013092,-0.004497,-0.019280,-0.029731,0.001453,-0.076674,0.013788,0.052292,-0.116965,-0.007136,0.059124,0.024886,-0.019830,0.002794,-0.076419,-0.032512,-0.055463,-0.030178,0.078000,0.021630,-0.052413,-0.080052,-0.017429,-0.003757,-0.015991,0.017957,0.126156,-0.013309,-0.065737,0.005441,0.005323,-0.089435,0.068350,-0.040247,-0.049179,0.021578,0.019738,-0.016526,0.063398,-0.045874,-0.105884,-0.005213,-0.026266,-0.087489,0.033579,-0.080427,0.086820,0.073841,-0.037830,-0.007492,0.066205,0.034970,-0.107647,0.010460,-0.074155,-0.006779,-0.014220,-0.057144,-0.050719,-0.076905,-0.062849,0.068555,0.021846,0.057021,-0.068510,0.052959,-0.001553,0.008643,-0.043777,-0.039813,0.044794,-0.009003,-0.002121,-0.046301,0.040814,-0.039759,0.052642,-0.004989,0.002755,0.038697,-0.098506,-0.025873,-0.000378,0.070774,0.