  ('X3','Escalation boundary - People track. Escalation. The single most important product-logic question is: at what point does a matter stop being safe for an SME to self-serve (with AI guidance, templates, checklists) and start requiring a human professional — consultant, employment lawyer, or registered HR practitioner? For "People" matters this boundary is reasonably well mapped by legal-commentary consensus: routine documentation, straightforward performance conversations and standard leave/entitlement questions are DIY-safe; anything involving termination with contested facts, discrimination, bullying/harassment complaints, restructures/redundancies, and enterprise agreements sits past the line.','[0.005691,-0.005165,-0.018518,-0.056232,0.063699,0.035814,0.021370,0.049473,-0.012271,-0.035891,-0.025087,0.027621,-0.037283,0.009908,0.095104,0.018719,0.007369,-0.017176,-0.056925,-0.037808,-0.044884,0.017036,-0.063039,0.004148,-0.114251,-0.065810,0.057090,0.001322,-0.016271,-0.075007,0.042485,-0.034342,0.005353,0.061722,0.005030,0.050499,0.049708,-0.018313,-0.026639,-0.045407,0.018506,-0.093977,-0.100266,-0.013761,0.031881,-0.006866,0.021331,-0.026103,-0.125377,-0.021970,-0.016715,-0.075289,-0.008288,0.128743,-0.056305,-0.024848,0.071035,0.000971,0.027241,0.012590,-0.007282,-0.036102,-0.047209,0.021338,0.083324,-0.026972,0.005145,0.052032,0.016312,0.075882,-0.009681,-0.112393,-0.031212,0.026037,0.057865,0.003537,-0.001305,0.013506,0.076177,-0.015142,0.024125,0.005998,-0.043766,0.051752,-0.050691,0.006964,-0.034193,0.017672,0.064602,0.073264,-0.034413,0.038184,0.113080,-0.025452,0.030701,-0.010686,-0.131281,-0.055444,-0.009287,0.005922,-0.071861,0.025727,0.013190,-0.011476,0.016767,-0.042076,-0.008896,0.002406,-0.035193,0.003016,-0.034255,-0.033325,0.022851,-0.093332,0.086316,-0.000403,-0.017297,0.087144,0.043010,-0.058495,0.006420,0.031222,-0.006018,-0.006512,0.008705,0.002738,-0.047882,0.000000,-0.038816,0.005586,-0.009994,0.084250,0.017707,0.024254,-0.038595,0.0